   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose a programmer inherits the <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ContractTax</code> class from class <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Tax</code> and wants to override <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Tax'</code>s <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">calc_tax()</code>. What should the programmer do?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1330030,
     "content_html": "Define another <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">calc_tax()</code> method in <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">Tax</code>.",
     "correctness": "0.0",
     "feedback_html": "The method definition should be in the subclass, not the superclass."
    },
    {
     "id": 1330031,
     "content_html": "Define a <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">calc_tax()</code> method in <code class=\"python\" data-lang=\"python\">ContractTax</code>.",
     "correctness": "1.0",
     "feedback_html": "Overriding involves defining a subclass method that has the same name as the superclass method."
